s":-0.00436489703855311,"_gp_accruals":true,"_score_accruals":7.9,"_gate_rev_volatility":1.2717125367301116,"_gp_rev_volatility":false,"_score_rev_volatility":0.0,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.18612600769940957,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":false,"_score_margin_vs_hist":0.0,"_gate_piotroski":6,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":66.7,"_gate_spread":0.12494031823684794,"_gp_spread":true,"_score_spread":62.5,"_gate_roic_consistency":1.8127432593776014,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":0.27807397303035425,"_gp_incr_roic":true,"_score_incr_roic":100.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.2995561180359142,"_gp_margin_advantage":true,"_score_margin_advantage":100.0,"_gate_pool_share":-0.18166431265488914,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":0.0,"_gate_rev_durability":0.5373486018963807,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":100.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":-0.06102984444652526,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0.03194105849861867,"_gp_fund_growth":true,"_score_fund_growth":31.9,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.05593877689957264,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":73.3,"_gate_share_shrink":0.010145570899018574,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":37.3,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.008059671605927113,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":86.6,"_gate_insider_own":0.0064,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":4.3,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Cheniere Energy, Inc., an energy infrastructure company, primarily engages in the liquefied natural gas (LNG) related businesses in the United States. The company owns and operates the Sabine Pass LNG terminal in Cameron Parish, Louisiana; and the Corpus Christi LNG terminal near Corpus Christi, Texas. It also owns and operates the Creole Trail pipeline, a 94-mile natural gas supply pipeline that interconnects the Sabine Pass LNG Terminal with several large interstate and intrastate pipelines; and the Corpus Christi pipeline, a 21-mile natural gas supply pipeline that interconnects the Corpus Christi LNG terminal with interstate and intrastate natural gas pipelines. In addition, the company engages in the LNG and natural gas marketing business. Cheniere Energy, Inc. was incorporated in 1983 and is headquartered in Houston, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jack A. Fusco | President, CEO & Chairman | Age 63 | Compensation: $6.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $11.6M ranks in the top quartile among Energy peers, improving at 39%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $1.4M of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $94K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Cheniere Energy, Inc. is a large-cap energy business with a $56.8B market cap on $20.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -16% over the past three years and +54% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome. Operating margins are expanding by +5.7pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 20% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 12-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $2.5B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 12 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.04\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 9.6\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 5.6% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 4.2\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Energy peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Carries a 63% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.6259329723401141},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Heavy insider selling (net $29.4M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-29440110.47},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Energy tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"The commodity cycle \u2014 revenue and free cash flow are ultimately hostage to a price the company does not set, and the long-run energy-transition arc adds a structural overhang.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Geopolitical supply shocks \u2014 wars, sanctions, and OPEC decisions create volatility that no hedging programme can fully neutralise.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 30% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Energy peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Energy sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 6% over 3 months","Energy ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Can Cheniere Energy (NYSE:LNG) Deliver On Its Raised Outlook?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/energy/can-cheniere-energy-nyselng-deliver-on-its-raised-outlook","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793910720.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.67,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["guidance"]},{"title":"QatarEnergy eyes more US LNG deals to shield supply from Mideast conflict - report","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/energy/articles/qatarenergy-eyes-more-us-lng-181315275.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793902395.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.557,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Qatar in Talks to Buy More US LNG, Diversify Supply Outside Persian Gulf","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/energy/articles/qatar-talks-buy-more-us-165623170.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793897783.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.382,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]},{"title":"Cheniere Energy (NYSE:LNG) Stock Rating Upgraded by Zacks Research","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/cheniere-energy-nyselng-stock-rating-upgraded-by-zacks-research.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793884269.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.758,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"3 LNG Stocks Investors Are Watching As Long Term Gas Contracts Return","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/energy/articles/3-lng-stocks-investors-watching-051934435.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793855974.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.814,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["product"]},{"titl