), so read it loosely.","Liquidity is deep, with about $471.6M traded a day.","In past sell-offs it fell 55% in the 2020 crash, 18% in the 2022 bear market and 97% in 2008."],"val":["The price sits above its DCF fair value of $216 (margin of safety -29%), so there is no valuation cushion.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 44%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $156 to $297 (P10-P90), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks expensive against Energy peers: P/E 19.8 vs 13.4, EV/EBITDA 11.1 vs 6.9 and P/FCF 23.1 vs 14.3 (sector median).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 17% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are mixed: an FCF yield of 4.3% (below the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 10.3% (vs the 8% bar).","The 21 covering analysts target $319 on average, 15% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 20% clears the cost of capital of 8.0% by 12pp, the mark of a value creator; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 1.81).","It converts 12% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 1.04x.","ROE of 67% is amplified by 6.0x balance-sheet leverage (DuPont), so ROIC is the cleaner read on the business.","Operating margin is running 19pp above its own historical average, a peak-margin risk if conditions normalise.","It spends 0.8% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is moderate at 2.1x net debt to EBITDA ($1.1B of cash against $22.8B of debt), above the 1.5x gate, with interest covered 9.6x.","The current ratio of 0.94 means short-term liabilities exceed current assets."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at -15.8% over 3 years, 16.4% over 5 years and 53.7% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 127%).","At current returns, reinvesting 16% of profits supports about 3.2% a year of fundamental growth, enough to sustain growth.","Margins are expanding (+5.7% trend).","Forward indicators: a book-to-bill of 0.96, a backlog worth 11.2x annual revenue and deferred revenue down 8%.","Capex runs 2.3x depreciation (15.4% of sales), so it is building capacity for future growth.","Its Rule of 40 score is 28, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.6%), and institutions hold 93%.","Insiders have only sold over the past year (7 sales, net $29.4M sold).","It returns 5.6% a year to shareholders (4.8% in buybacks and 0.9% in dividends).","The share count has grown 1.0% a year over five years, diluting existing holders."],"people":["With about 1,717 employees, each generates about $11.6M of revenue, 5.7x the Energy median, and productivity has risen 39.4% a year.","That works out to $1.4M of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $6.4M (1x revenue per employee).","Stock compensation averages $94K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"WATCH","conv":59,"head":"Watch: priced 29% above its $216 fair value, but that value is low-confidence and the price is inside its $156\u2013$297 range.","pros":["ROIC 20.5% vs WACC 8.0%","FCF margin 12.3%","Revenue grew 16.4%/yr over 5y","12-1 month momentum +34%","Operating margin expanding 5.7%/yr"],"cons":["Trades 29% above fair value of $216","P/E 19.8x vs sector 13.4x","EV/EBITDA 11.1x vs sector 6.9x","P/FCF 23.1x vs sector 14.3x"],"flags":[],"need":["the model rates it HOLD","no margin of safety"],"buy_below":183.24,"vc":{"base":215.58,"base_src":"dcf","bear":156.19,"bull":296.74,"alt_median":333.59,"n_alt":3,"gap":-0.1449,"dispersion":0.4373,"level":"LOW","why":["models disagree (44% dispersion)"]},"med":{"pe":13.3952,"ev_ebitda":6.86,"pfcf":14.299,"pb":1.6885,"roic":0.0952,"gross_margin":0.2462,"fcf_margin":0.0754,"div_yield":0.0371}},"ticker":"LNG","date":"2026-11-06"}